  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates the skewness of the lotteries, specifically whether a greater portion of probability is assigned to favorable (positive) outcomes compared to unfavorable (negative) ones. A lottery is left-skewed if more probability is on the favorable side. In this case, Lottery A has a certain outcome of -3000 Euros (100% probability), meaning all outcomes are unfavorable. Lottery B has an 80% chance of -4000 Euros (unfavorable) and a 20% chance of 0 Euros (neutral, not favorable). Thus, Lottery B has a smaller portion of probability on favorable outcomes (20%) compared to unfavorable (80%). Therefore, Lottery B is right-skewed (more weight on unfavorable outcomes), and Lottery A is left-skewed only in a trivial sense (no favorable outcomes), or actually, it is not left-skewed at all. In fact, since both lotteries have no positive outcomes, the only possible favorable outcome is zero. In Lottery B, 20% of the probability is on zero (neutral), which is not favorable, so the favorable portion is zero. Thus, neither lottery has a significant favorable portion. However, the reason defines left-skew as greater probability on favorable outcomes. Since both lotteries have no positive outcomes, neither is left-skewed. Therefore, the decision reason cannot be applied meaningfully to this decision problem — there is no left-skewed lottery. Hence, the reason is not applicable in this context.",
  "step_2": "The verbal report contains only the phrase 'insgesamt am besten', which translates to 'overall best' in German. This is a vague statement and does not describe any specific reasoning process, such as evaluating outcomes, probabilities, or skewness. There is no information about how the individual considered the probabilities, outcomes, or any statistical feature like skewness. The individual does not explain the criteria used to compare the lotteries or justify the choice based on any rule, such as skewness. Therefore, the deliberation process described is not transparent or specific enough to identify the use of any particular decision reason.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating skewness — specifically, whether a greater portion of probability is assigned to favorable outcomes. In this case, neither lottery has a favorable outcome (positive value). Lottery A has a certain -3000 outcome (no favorable), and Lottery B has 80% chance of -4000 and 20% chance of 0, so no positive outcomes. Thus, both lotteries have zero favorable outcomes, so neither is left-skewed. Therefore, the decision reason is not applicable. Additionally, the verbal report provides no mention of skewness, favorable outcomes, or any reasoning related to probability distribution shape. The individual simply states 'insgesamt am besten', which lacks any explicit or implicit reference to skewness. Since the reason cannot be applied and is not referenced in the report, the individual did not use the decision reason. The assessment is therefore 0.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
